{"id":"evil-merodach","name":"Evil-Merodach","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:evil-merodach"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Evil-merodach","text":"Merodach’s man, the son and successor of Nebuchadnezzar, king of Babylon (2 Kings 25:27; Jer. 52:31, 34). He seems to have reigned but two years (B.C. 562-560). Influenced probably by Daniel, he showed kindness to Jehoiachin, who had been a prisoner in Babylon for thirty-seven years. He released him, and “spoke kindly to him.” He was murdered by Nergal-sharezer=Neriglissar, his brother-in-law, who succeeded him (Jer. 39:3, 13)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H894","lemma":"בָּבֶל","xlit":"Bâbel","gloss":"Babel , including Babylonia and the Babylonian empire","kjv":"Babel, Babylon","count":5,"share":0.63},{"strong":"H8548","lemma":"תָּמִיד","xlit":"tâmîyd","gloss":"continuance","kjv":"alway, continual, daily, ever","count":4,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H192","lemma":"אֱוִיל מְרֹדַךְ","xlit":"ʼĔvîyl Mᵉrôdak","gloss":"Evil-Merodak, a Babylonian king","kjv":"Evil-merodach","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H737","lemma":"אֲרֻחָה","xlit":"ʼăruchâh","gloss":"a ration of food","kjv":"allowance, diet, dinner, victuals","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H3608","lemma":"כֶּלֶא","xlit":"keleʼ","gloss":"a prison","kjv":"prison","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H3078","lemma":"יְהוֹיָכִין","xlit":"Yᵉhôwyâkîyn","gloss":"Jehojakin, a Jewish king","kjv":"Jehoiachin","count":2,"share":0.25}],"verses":["2Kgs.25.27","2Kgs.25.28","Jer.52.31","Jer.52.32","Jer.52.34","2Kgs.25.29","2Kgs.25.30","Jer.52.33"],"related":[{"id":"jehoiachin","type":"cooccur","shared":8,"jaccard":0.195,"why":"8 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"captive","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.043,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"kindness","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.02,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"babylon","type":"lexical","strong":"H894","why":"both lead with בָּבֶל (H894)"},{"id